{"run_id":"run_a33573abb22b","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"The **Diligence material handling standard** is short. Its rules are:\n\n1. **Diligence material is compartmented.** Access is limited to specific people, not open to everyone who has internal access.\n2. **Each artifact lists its named reviewers.** Every diligence document or file records who is authorised to review it.\n3. **Sharing outside that list needs approval.** Before the material goes to anyone not on the named list, the workstream owner has to approve it.\n4. **The standard itself holds no diligence content.** It only describes the process.\n\nIn practice, check the named-reviewer list on the artifact before you share it. If the person you want to share with isn't on it, get the workstream owner's approval first. The standard doesn't say how owners are identified. The *Project Halyard workstream index* (res://docs/internal/halyard-workstream-index) may list them, but I haven't checked.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
